# Step 30, part 2: the registry's kinds of source and held tools, a
# server's tool as the registry holds it (`McpTool`), section 6 from the
# registry in every build, the round's cache of early results, and the
# check of a build without the MCP client
# (docs/steps/30/parts/pr2-registry-tool.md).

# --- The registry: kinds of source --------------------------------------------

[break] a-name-of-the-other-kind-is-taken
rule: A source of one kind is refused a name a source of the other kind holds, so an MCP server and an extension never replace each other's tools.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/registry.rs
in: ToolRegistry::set_source_with_holds
find: && holder != kind
replace: && false
caught-by:
    cineris-tools::it registry::a_source_of_the_other_kind_never_takes_a_name_or_removes_its_tools

[break] a-removal-reaches-the-other-kind
rule: Removing a source removes only a source of its own kind.
file: crates/cineris-tools/src/registry.rs
in: ToolRegistry::remove_source
find: sources.get(source).is_some_and(|held| held.kind == kind)
replace: sources.get(source).is_some()
caught-by:
    cineris-tools::it registry::a_source_of_the_other_kind_never_takes_a_name_or_removes_its_tools

